 "description": "Second CNN screening, 3 seeds per configuration (night 1 showed that single-seed gains did not hold up). 300 random configurations near what worked on night 1 (32 to 64 mel bands, mean or mean + SD pooling, SpecAugment, class weighting), adding settings not varied before: per-speaker normalization, the learning-rate schedule, warmup, early-stopping patience, the epoch cap, and finer learning-rate and weight-decay steps. Left out after night 1: 80 and 128 mel bands, the 50 ms window, the 4 kHz cutoff, 3 and 10 s crops, soft labels, 2 convolutions per block, 5x5 kernels, max and attention pooling, batch 64. Stage random (100 configurations, priority 50) is the planned screening. Stage random_extra (200 more, priority 20) keeps the GPUs busy through the weekend night: it uses the same sampling seed and space, so its generator repeats the first 100 draws, skips them as already present, and continues with the next 200 (the same configurations as n_configs 300 in one stage). Priority 20 puts it after every other sweep of the night. Runs after cnn_confirm_1. Validation only.",
